From acb133c0780be880b0434665baf892a5c001069a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 01:32:22 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] kcm_energyinfo: one details form with noun sections;
 batteries are scanned after the first frame

Page type: Info/Form (docs/page-design.md 2): device buttons (when more than one battery), history graph with its
controls, then the facts. The facts (Battery, Energy, Environment) were three FormLayouts tied together with
twinFormLayouts and a Heading-level-2 hack that hid a title when all rows were empty; now one Kirigami.FormLayout with
Kirigami.Separator sections (isSection), the same section look as the other pages; a section title is hidden when none of
its rows has a value (hasValues(), a real binding instead of itemAt()). The rows, labels and formatters are unchanged, so no
aliases. History graph, Charge Percentage / Energy Consumption, Timespan, Refresh unchanged. Markers: all 9 rows
(kcm_energyinfo/*); inventory_check --kcm kcm_energyinfo --strict: 0 lost.

Speed (cause found in code): BatteryModel's constructor ran Solid::Device::listFromType(Battery) and a sort that reads
isPowerSupply() and product() of every battery, and connected Solid::DeviceNotifier::instance() (sets up Solid's
backends), all during page creation (kcm.cpp:38). Now BatteryModel::populate() runs from the event loop, inserting the rows
as one insertion (not a reset, so the list keeps currentIndex 0) and setting the new "loaded" property; the "No energy
information available" placeholder waits for loaded so it does not flash. The history is already asynchronous (UPower via
QDBusPendingCallWatcher). After numbers: pending, manager will measure.

Not built yet. Uncertain: Component with required properties used as Repeater delegate under "pragma ComponentBehavior:
Bound" (same required properties as the old inline delegate); QList::removeIf needs Qt 6.1 (fine for 6.8+).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
